{
  "name": "Expired Listings Monitor",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "hours",
              "hour": 6
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [240, 300],
      "id": "schedule-6am",
      "name": "Daily 6 AM"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "search",
        "base": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "={{ $env.AIRTABLE_BASE_ID }}",
          "mode": "id"
        },
        "table": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "Settings",
          "mode": "name"
        },
        "filterByFormula": "={Key} = 'target_cities'"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.airtable",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [460, 300],
      "id": "get-cities",
      "name": "Get Target Cities",
      "credentials": {
        "airtableTokenApi": {
          "id": "airtable-creds",
          "name": "Airtable"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Parse cities for expired listing search\n// Note: Expired listings are best sourced from:\n// 1. MLS API (if you have access)\n// 2. Zillow 'Off Market' with recent price history\n// 3. Realtor.com 'Off Market'\n// 4. Third-party data providers (PropStream, BatchLeads)\n\nconst settings = $input.first()?.json?.fields || {};\nlet cities = ['Austin'];\n\nif (settings.Value) {\n  try {\n    cities = JSON.parse(settings.Value);\n  } catch (e) {\n    cities = settings.Value.split(',').map(c => c.trim());\n  }\n}\n\nreturn cities.map(city => ({\n  json: {\n    city: city,\n    state: 'TX',\n    // Zillow off-market search\n    zillow_url: `https://www.zillow.com/${city.toLowerCase().replace(/ /g, '-')}-tx/recently-sold/`,\n    // Days to look back\n    days_back: 7\n  }\n}));"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [680, 300],
      "id": "prepare-searches",
      "name": "Prepare Searches"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "batchSize": 1,
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.splitInBatches",
      "typeVersion": 3,
      "position": [900, 300],
      "id": "loop-cities",
      "name": "Loop Cities"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "={{ $json.zillow_url }}",
        "authentication": "none",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "User-Agent",
              "value": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "responseFormat": "text"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [1120, 260],
      "id": "scrape-zillow",
      "name": "Scrape Zillow Off-Market",
      "continueOnFail": true
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Parse expired/withdrawn listings from Zillow\nconst html = $input.first().json.data || $input.first().json.body || '';\nconst cityData = $('Loop Cities').item.json;\n\nlet listings = [];\n\ntry {\n  // Look for properties that were listed but didn't sell (withdrawn/expired)\n  // Zillow shows these in 'Off Market' or 'Recently Sold' sections\n  \n  // Try to find embedded JSON data\n  const jsonMatch = html.match(/\"listResults\"\\s*:\\s*(\\[[\\s\\S]*?\\])/);\n  if (jsonMatch) {\n    const data = JSON.parse(jsonMatch[1]);\n    listings = data\n      .filter(item => {\n        // Look for expired indicators\n        const status = (item.statusType || item.listingStatus || '').toLowerCase();\n        const statusText = (item.statusText || '').toLowerCase();\n        return status.includes('off market') || \n               status.includes('withdrawn') ||\n               status.includes('expired') ||\n               statusText.includes('off market');\n      })\n      .map(item => ({\n        address: item.address || item.streetAddress,\n        city: item.city || cityData.city,\n        state: item.state || cityData.state,\n        zip: item.zipcode,\n        price: item.price || item.unformattedPrice,\n        original_list_price: item.price,\n        bedrooms: item.beds,\n        bathrooms: item.baths,\n        sqft: item.area,\n        listing_url: item.detailUrl ? `https://www.zillow.com${item.detailUrl}` : '',\n        zestimate: item.zestimate,\n        days_on_market: item.daysOnZillow || 0,\n        status_reason: 'Expired/Withdrawn',\n        source: 'Expired MLS',\n        scraped_at: new Date().toISOString()\n      }));\n  }\n} catch (e) {\n  console.log('Parse error:', e.message);\n}\n\n// If direct parsing fails, try alternative approach\nif (listings.length === 0) {\n  // Create placeholder entries that can be enriched\n  // In production, use MLS API or data provider\n  const addressMatches = html.match(/\"streetAddress\"\\s*:\\s*\"([^\"]+)\"/g) || [];\n  \n  for (let i = 0; i < Math.min(addressMatches.length, 20); i++) {\n    const address = addressMatches[i]?.match(/\"([^\"]+)\"$/)?.[1];\n    if (address) {\n      listings.push({\n        address: address,\n        city: cityData.city,\n        state: cityData.state,\n        source: 'Expired MLS',\n        status_reason: 'Potential Expired',\n        scraped_at: new Date().toISOString()\n      });\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nreturn listings.map(l => ({ json: l }));"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [1340, 260],
      "id": "parse-expired",
      "name": "Parse Expired Listings"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict"
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "has-address",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.address }}",
              "rightValue": "",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "notEmpty"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.filter",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [1560, 260],
      "id": "filter-valid",
      "name": "Filter Valid Addresses"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "search",
        "base": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "={{ $env.AIRTABLE_BASE_ID }}",
          "mode": "id"
        },
        "table": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "Leads",
          "mode": "name"
        },
        "filterByFormula": "=AND({Address} = '{{ $json.address }}', {City} = '{{ $json.city }}')"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.airtable",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [1780, 260],
      "id": "check-dup",
      "name": "Check Duplicate",
      "credentials": {
        "airtableTokenApi": {
          "id": "airtable-creds",
          "name": "Airtable"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict"
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "is-new",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.records?.length }}",
              "rightValue": 0,
              "operator": {
                "type": "number",
                "operation": "equals"
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [2000, 260],
      "id": "is-new",
      "name": "Is New?"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "create",
        "base": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "={{ $env.AIRTABLE_BASE_ID }}",
          "mode": "id"
        },
        "table": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "Leads",
          "mode": "name"
        },
        "fields": {
          "fieldMapping": [
            {
              "fieldName": "Address",
              "fieldValue": "={{ $('Filter Valid Addresses').item.json.address }}"
            },
            {
              "fieldName": "City",
              "fieldValue": "={{ $('Filter Valid Addresses').item.json.city }}"
            },
            {
              "fieldName": "State",
              "fieldValue": "={{ $('Filter Valid Addresses').item.json.state }}"
            },
            {
              "fieldName": "ZIP",
              "fieldValue": "={{ $('Filter Valid Addresses').item.json.zip }}"
            },
            {
              "fieldName": "Asking Price",
              "fieldValue": "={{ $('Filter Valid Addresses').item.json.price || $('Filter Valid Addresses').item.json.original_list_price }}"
            },
            {
              "fieldName": "Estimated Value",
              "fieldValue": "={{ $('Filter Valid Addresses').item.json.zestimate || $('Filter Valid Addresses').item.json.price }}"
            },
            {
              "fieldName": "Source",
              "fieldValue": "Expired MLS"
            },
            {
              "fieldName": "Status",
              "fieldValue": "New"
            },
            {
              "fieldName": "Listing URL",
              "fieldValue": "={{ $('Filter Valid Addresses').item.json.listing_url }}"
            },
            {
              "fieldName": "Priority",
              "fieldValue": "High"
            },
            {
              "fieldName": "Notes",
              "fieldValue": "=Expired/Withdrawn listing - HIGH MOTIVATION. Original DOM: {{ $('Filter Valid Addresses').item.json.days_on_market || 'Unknown' }}"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.airtable",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [2220, 220],
      "id": "create-lead",
      "name": "Create Lead (Priority: High)",
      "credentials": {
        "airtableTokenApi": {
          "id": "airtable-creds",
          "name": "Airtable"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "channel": "#hot-leads",
        "text": "=:rotating_light: *Expired Listing Found!*\n\n*Property:* {{ $('Filter Valid Addresses').item.json.address }}, {{ $('Filter Valid Addresses').item.json.city }}\n*Original Price:* ${{ $('Filter Valid Addresses').item.json.price?.toLocaleString() || 'Unknown' }}\n*Days on Market:* {{ $('Filter Valid Addresses').item.json.days_on_market || 'Unknown' }}\n\n:fire: *High motivation seller - listing expired/withdrawn!*\n\nThis lead has been added with HIGH priority for immediate enrichment.",
        "otherOptions": {}
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.slack",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [2440, 220],
      "id": "slack-alert",
      "name": "Slack Alert (Expired = Gold)",
      "credentials": {
        "slackApi": {
          "id": "slack-creds",
          "name": "Slack"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "amount": "={{ Math.floor(Math.random() * 3) + 1 }}",
        "unit": "seconds"
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.wait",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [2660, 260],
      "id": "delay",
      "name": "Random Delay",
      "webhookId": "expired-delay"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [2220, 340],
      "id": "skip-dup",
      "name": "Skip Duplicate"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [2880, 300],
      "id": "done",
      "name": "Done"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Expired Listings Monitor\n\n**Why Expired = GOLD:**\n- Owner already tried to sell (proven motivation)\n- Frustrated with previous agent\n- Ready to try again\n- 15-25% conversion rate!\n\n**Best Sources:**\n1. MLS API (if licensed)\n2. PropStream or BatchLeads\n3. Zillow 'Off Market'\n4. Realtor.com status changes\n\n**This workflow sets Priority = High**",
        "height": 280,
        "width": 380,
        "color": 4
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [200, 40],
      "id": "sticky-note",
      "name": "Why Expired Listings"
    }
  ],
